      "body": "@sashikamw: I don't think we need to remove names from the comment. Because anyone can comment any other person's name there. So it does not mean that he/she put their name. For an example, let's say I'm a user of this system and I put your name there. But you are not an actual user of the system, hence we cannot identify the actual person from this comment.\r\n\r\nFor as another example, Let's say, someone put your name on the comment, but that person's intention is not to point you, but to point someone else who has the same name. For this scenario also, just by looking at the comment, we cannot identify the real user.",
